{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/919741-dark-wars-2-world-war-2-in-world-of-darkness","id":919741,"title":"Dark Wars 2 - World War 2 in World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-23T08:51:00-07:00","id":919741,"title":"Dark Wars 2 - World War 2 in World of Darkness","content":"I'm a World War 2 buff, so this topic is partially my thing along with those like me, and partially inspiried by last night's episode of Nova about the discovery of U-166.<br /> <br /> While Wraith has The Great War (at least as a historical setting). I've seen limited resources or info about WW2. Most that I've seen covered is from character backstory (mainly the Vampires from the VTMYTE game) and what random bits and pieces that is hinted at like the Get's involvement on both sides of the war. Mortal Timeline and equipment shouldn't be that hard to track down and convert. But supernatural involvement would be since I know during the time period not many were as active as others, Mummies and Demons proper for sure wouldn't be involved. Others would take it as personal preference or duty to country or the right cause.<br /> <br /> Vampire - Primarily served as personal preference. Axis Vampires would take the death camps and the Third Reich as a Godsend for free food and the military machine cranking out resources. Allied Vampires would play politics to try to suede the powers to rise up in arms since a Nazi controlled Europe would be a Sabbat feasting ground. Soviet Vampires would be part of resistance groups sprinkled around Russia during occupation and major conflicts like Stalingrad or picking off Nazi soldiers on the battlefields like Kursk.<br /> Werewolf - Practically a civil war. Part of the Get of Fenris serving Nazi Germany and the Third Reich doesn't help things either. Packs mobilize to help Allied efforts, serving Army and Naval forces. Other breeds filling out rank and file for ground, naval, and air forces. Many fetishes were created from the gear to even vehicles (tanks, planes, ships, subs). These vehicular fetishes gain much renown and still serve in Battleground.<br /> Mage - Shit hit the fan, no doubt about that. Traditions, Technocrats, and Disparates all serve both sides. Either as rank and file soldiers proper, resistance fighters, engineers, doctors, pilots, naval captains. You name it, there's a Mage somewhere. Technocrats playing both sides to keep sleepers under their heel while in-fighting split the Technocracy creating two rogue factions that lead to two new Traditions.<br /> Wraith - Finally recovered from the scars of The Great War. War spills back into the Shadowlands. New Relics, Wraiths, and Spectres pour forth from all fronts like a rushing river. The Dark Kingdoms has a hard time readjusting to their new population boosts, but their fighting continues as the Dark Kingdom of Iron engages with the Dark Kingdom of Jade as soldiers fight on knowing only their orders from the mortal coil. Hierarchy for both sides try to resolve their differences but ultimately fails as the fighting continues.<br /> Hunters - None of the Imbued are known to be active at the time. Mortal Hunters are either soldiers who happened upon the supernatural either on the front, between engagements, or even resistance fighters finding &quot;vultures&quot; amongst the ruins of the cities or occupied areas.<br /> Kuei-Jin - Total civil war. Mainland Jin combat those of the Empire of Japan when hostilities began. Imperial Jin serving as soldiers, naval forces, and pilots, while mainland Jin soldiers, tankers, and resistance. Mainland Jin allying themselves with the Beast Courts and other Allied forces when situations gotten desperate, but Allied forces being the hardest to gain support since for the longest while the fighting was focused in Europe.<br /> Earthbound - Reawakened when members of the Third Reich stumbled upon a couple of Earthbound Reliquaries. It is rumored that the SS and the Thule Society serve Earthbound entities. Unsure of the claims yet. But one thing is for sure, something has woken up with fighting spread out over land, sea, and air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:41:25-07:00","id":919769,"title":"","content":"Vampire - It's all going to matter which side you're on. Axis Toreadors who benefit from the Nazi's massive art heist are probably ga-ga.The Ravnos and Gangrel associated with the Gypsies probably don't see the death camps as a godsend. Also, unless you are running the place (like say some German Ventrue might), they are heavily regulated and guarded. Stealth would be a high priority if the Masquerade matters. The conflict between Nazi sympathizing vampires and, Hell, Nazi's proper and the more old school Tzimisce isn't going to be friendly at all. Is there anything about what Baba Yaga is up to? That could definitely affect what would be going on between the Soviet Brujah and the Nazi-sympathizer Ventrue types. <br /> Wraith - There is definitely some information about what happened in WWII in the Shoah book. <br /> Mage - There is definitely a slide towards the Nephandi in the Third Reich. To the point the Allied side of the Technocracy and Tradtions were willing to exercise a limited and inconstant truce to face the problem. Even if you are a Tradition mage who LOVES the Nazis for some reason (Nordic Verbena, Iteration-X for the German military tech and production surge, some Etherites with the wilder SCIENCE-y stuff the Nazis got up to, Voormas-like Euthanatos, Mengele-like Progenitors, Himmler-friendly Hermetics, etc.) there is definitely going to be an ethical slide towards the dark side, even if actual outright corruption, through-the-Cauls Nephandi status isn't reached). All in all, it seems like the time when you are most likely to get WILDLY mixed up cabals on both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:48:43-07:00","id":919773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage - Shit hit the fan, no doubt about that. Traditions, Technocrats, and Disparates all serve both sides. Either as rank and file soldiers proper, resistance fighters, engineers, doctors, pilots, naval captains. You name it, there's a Mage somewhere. Technocrats playing both sides to keep sleepers under their heel while in-fighting split the Technocracy creating two rogue factions that lead to two new Traditions. </div> </div> </div>Actually the SoE left the Technocracy before WWI and had become a full member of the Traditions by this point. The VA are still members of the Union but they don't leave until after the war.<br /> <br /> Also the Technocracy at first backed the Axis powers but once it became apparent just Nephandi-corrupted they had become as well as the massive surge of Nephandi, led to them not just abandoning the Axis for the Allies but teaming up with the Traditions because things had gotten so bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraith - Finally recovered from the scars of The Great War. War spills back into the Shadowlands. New Relics, Wraiths, and Spectres pour forth from all fronts like a rushing river. The Dark Kingdoms has a hard time readjusting to their new population boosts, but their fighting continues as the Dark Kingdom of Iron engages with the Dark Kingdom of Jade as soldiers fight on knowing only their orders from the mortal coil. Hierarchy for both sides try to resolve their differences but ultimately fails as the fighting continues. </div> </div> </div>And the horrors of the Holocaust and the rise of the Covenant of Millions. Regardless of what one might think about <i>Charnel Houses</i>, one cannot deny that the horrors of the Holocaust would have noticeable impact on the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:34:36-07:00","id":919801,"title":"","content":"The numbers of the Swords of Heimdall probably wouldn't have split the Get of Fenris numbers down the middle. Probably not even if you just count the Fenrir numbers in Europe. The Swords were not particularly keen on expanding their qualifiers for membership, and since Revised and especially in W20, the tribe as a whole became much more diverse in its array of human kin, while most camps were presented as being extremely small fringe groups.<br /> <br /> That aside, Garou tribes don't obey human territorial borders. That's why you have nearly everyone but the Fianna in Russia, and not just Silver Fangs. Similarly, there would have been an awful lot of other tribes, particularly Glass Walkers, living in the cities when the Nazis came to power, and the Glass Walkers were much more likely to hold positions in human society. This leads to some... troubling conclusions about what Cockroach's tribe would have been up to in those years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-23-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:59:21-07:00","id":920220,"title":"","content":"Here's a few 100% canonical events that take place in and around WW2. Specific citations available on request.<br /> The Brujah are behind Stalin signing he Molotov-Ribbentrov Pact.<br /> The Jovian Veterans are reactivated by the Void Engineers to fight Nephandi.<br /> 90% of the Hagalaz are killed battling Nazi Magi.<br /> The NWO formally puts its support behind Hitler on January 4, 1940.<br /> VA's denounce Hitler on October 15, 1941, and then make sure Pearl Harbour happens as a 'surprise' in December so that America will be fired up enough to enter the war.<br /> 1941 also sees the full schism between Nazi and Russian Get, presumably also non-Nazi German Get. Bone Gnawers are why half the population of Leningrad survived the siege.<br /> 1942 and 43 sees Situation Six form to fight the Nazi mages, the Hierarchy issue a call for all free Reapers to go to Europe, and the Euthanatoi start covertly pushing the Traditions to the Allied side by assassinating prominent pro-Axis Traditionalists, and the first Matter Transmission Portals developed.<br /> 44 sees the LA Anarch revolt and also the Technocracy as a whole officially turning on the Nazis. 45 continues to distract America's cainites by seeing major offensives by the Anarch revolutionaries, while Sabbat tzimisce use the chaos in Europe to being a 4 year process of conquering all of Romania.<br /> Garou storm Berlin alongside the Russians and so do the Technocrat-Traditionalist Alliance Forces.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:50:57-07:00","id":920369,"title":"","content":"Ajax - Haven't had time yet to double check on Baba Yaga. I got the Rage across Russia book, but still trying to figure out bills.<br /> AkatsukiLeader - From what I've read of SoE that the split happened during WW2. The one thing I knew for sure and forgot to post was SoE had control of Pangaea/Hollow Earth until the Technocracy sealed it off. Also working my way around to the Holocaust, soldiers and resistance fighters was the easiest one to figure out. With bills, haven't had time to go into the death camps in depth yet.<br /> Saur Ops - I knew there were some that served on the Axis, and from what I've read the Get were primarily Allied. Territories wasn't and issue since if you were actively serving you knew where the front is. Packs in resistance groups would still worry about territory, but it would be more relaxed since your main goal is driving out the occupying force.<br /> loomer - Do you happen to have years for the Brujah, Jovaian Vets, and the Hagalaz massacre?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T08:26:01-07:00","id":920378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/919741-dark-wars-2-world-war-2-in-world-of-darkness?p=920369#post920369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AkatsukiLeader - From what I've read of SoE that the split happened during WW2.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sons of Ether (formerly Electrodyne Engineers) joined the Traditions in 1905 to fill the seat of Matter left vacant by the Solificati because the Technocratic Union removed the concept of Ether from their Consensus in 1904, its referenced in Sons of Ether Traditionbook page 21, the removal of Ether being specifically mentioned in NWO's Lord Craven's letter concerning stopping the rebelliousness of the 'Sons of Ether' among the Electrodyne Engineers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T08:37:56-07:00","id":920385,"title":"","content":"I'll look that up as soon as I can get too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:18:17-07:00","id":920403,"title":"","content":"Cynic01 is 100% right about the SoE and their joining the Eight Traditions, (which was the number for a long time as the Solificati were out way way way back (1470) after the First Cabal debacle and the Seat of Matter was vacant for a substantial period). Then it was back down to Eight when the Ahl-i-Batin left in 1922. So it was Eight, not Nine Traditions for the duration of the War and the years that led up to it.<br /> <br /> The VA's were still a part of the Union for the duration of the War. Their position is very likely to be almost entirely Allied proponents, considering Turing's position in the Convention, Bletchley Park and where the next significant steps in computing are going to happen (the US). The VA's left the Union (1956), after the NWO's attempted (successful?) assassination of Turing (1954), were on their own for a very short scary time and then joined the Traditions (1961) offering up a copy of the Time Table. Which made it the Nine Traditions again for only the 3rd time (1466-1470, 1905-1922, 1961-present) and just in time for the Pogrom to go into full swing for the heart of the Cold War.<br /> <br /> That also means it was Six Conventions - the Virtual Adepts, the relatively new NWO (1920), Progenitors, Syndicate, Void Engineers, and Iteration-X (which may have still been called IBM, but I can't pin down a firm date on when the Computer achieved sentience.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-24-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:45:45-07:00","id":920540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/919741-dark-wars-2-world-war-2-in-world-of-darkness#post919741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a World War 2 buff, so this topic is partially my thing along with those like me, and partially inspiried by last night's episode of Nova about the discovery of U-166.<br /> <br /> While Wraith has The Great War (at least as a historical setting). I've seen limited resources or info about WW2. Most that I've seen covered is from character backstory (mainly the Vampires from the VTMYTE game) and what random bits and pieces that is hinted at like the Get's involvement on both sides of the war. Mortal Timeline and equipment shouldn't be that hard to track down and convert. But supernatural involvement would be since I know during the time period not many were as active as others, Mummies and Demons proper for sure wouldn't be involved. Others would take it as personal preference or duty to country or the right cause.<br /> <br /> ..Snip..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in many films/marvel comics, we see some groups of various governments having used 'superpowered individuals' as sort of special ops shock troops..<br /> So i could potentially see a group of &quot;Knowing&quot; uppers, having a secret pack or two of garou under their sway.. And the Delerium would help keep what they did from being public knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T14:16:39-07:00","id":920559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/919741-dark-wars-2-world-war-2-in-world-of-darkness?p=920369#post920369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ajax - Haven't had time yet to double check on Baba Yaga. I got the Rage across Russia book, but still trying to figure out bills.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC in the canon setting she was in torpor from the late 10th century to 1991.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T17:19:23-07:00","id":920643,"title":"","content":"Which is why I want to double check Baba Yaga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T08:35:34-07:00","id":920973,"title":"","content":"On the Mage issue again, particularly the Technocracy, we've been dealing with an aspect of this in my current M20 game. All the PCs are partially amnesiac and time-displaced. One of them is a '40s era Virtual Adept. One of the issues we face in dealing with Union (and some Etherite) characters is what does advanced tech MEAN in the past? Is it just what was ended up actually happening? Or does it deal with what the people of the time considered &quot;futuristic&quot;? (Which means, interestingly, some things that would have been in use by Technocrats might have ended up later being Etherite SCIENCE tech...) <br /> <br /> We've split the difference. Some of the things are what actually happened. After all, there is a Time Table. So some of his computer tech is &quot;super-early-adopter&quot; stuff that wouldn't show up for decades (10-20 years for most, but up to 40 years ahead of its time here and there). But some of his stuff is straight out what was current sci-fi of the day. After all, a VA that needs a computer that takes up a large room to do anything wouldn't be very much fun to play, especially from the POV of a highly mobile game. (Though having the same VA using that computer remotely via, say, hardline telephone and radio broadcasts, is sorta interesting....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:11:20-07:00","id":921236,"title":"","content":"I think dieselpunk, Rayburn Gothic, and early atomicpunk. Power armor, energy weapons, VTOL, primitive space exploration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T19:45:08-07:00","id":921308,"title":"","content":"Not so primitive, I think. The Y122 is from 1944.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T07:30:20-07:00","id":921476,"title":"","content":"At least it doesn't look like spelljammer ships like in sorcerer's crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T08:22:39-07:00","id":921499,"title":"","content":"Now I want to see a general source book for this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:06:45-07:00","id":921513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/919741-dark-wars-2-world-war-2-in-world-of-darkness?p=921236#post921236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think dieselpunk, Rayburn Gothic, and early atomicpunk. Power armor, energy weapons, VTOL, primitive space exploration.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those would definitely work for SoE concepts but a lot wouldn't really scan with the Union. A bit here and there (like VTOL). Some slices of the &quot;out there&quot; projects both sides were researching during the War. Turing's computer = Union tech. Bat-bombs = SoE. But there are significant differences in fundamentals and a lot is really under dealt with. No Digital Web. The VA's go-to is using radio waves and hard-lines to affect things at a distance (i.e. Correspondence). There are already battles going on in space between Etherites and the VE's.<br /> <br /> Just coming up with what a character is carrying around to use as their Instruments is an exercise in creativity. Our 1940's VA's main Instrument is something that looks like one of those portable radio sets used by soldiers during WWII. It has some significant modifications, which involve some mental gymnastics all their own. Under the phone headset in the top is a slot for a &quot;card-drive&quot;, a mechanical magazine full of punch cards to run different sua-programs. It can also be configured to put a blank set of cards in and punch in the data. Pop off the front and there's a reel-to-reel magnetic tape set up. There's a sliding panel on the side which uncovers a screen adjacent to slides and dials which looks something like an oscilloscope. He was wearing something that looks like the equipment belt a phone repairmen going up a pole wears (with an additional selection of electronics tools). And so on. It's something like what makes sense at the time mixed up with stuff that is definitely where things are going to be going (though in a more hectic fashion than the later streamlined tech the Masses will get) with a few dead ends that looks nonsensical or analogous to something out of the more &quot;hard science&quot; of the then current science fiction. Less what we think of what thing would be like than what THEY think things would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-27-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T19:19:59-07:00","id":921815,"title":"","content":"It would also fit the time and to them it's futuristic. If the Nazi power armor is any indication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-